    "text": "The temperature of an ideal gas is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> . If the <math><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></math> speed of the gas molecule is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> , then at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> it becomes",
